From d38f7b5d44533e696480b0bd90b150824eda3559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:28:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] BUG: Update all segmentation display nodes when segments are
 added or removed

When a segment was added to or removed from a segmentation, only the first
display node of the segmentation updated its segment list. Other display
nodes updated their list later, when their display properties were first
needed. Therefore, if a segment was removed and a new segment was added
with the same ID, the other display nodes applied the display properties of
the removed segment (for example, visibility) to the new segment.

Now all the display nodes of the segmentation update their segment list
when a segment is added or removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Libs/MRML/Core/Testing/CMakeLists.txt         |  2 +
 .../Testing/vtkMRMLSegmentationNodeTest1.cxx  | 83 +++++++++++++++++++
 Libs/MRML/Core/vtkMRMLSegmentationNode.cxx    | 28 ++++---
 3 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Libs/MRML/Core/Testing/vtkMRMLSegmentationNodeTest1.cxx

